course: dictionary
lesson: 1697
title: Chunks: pieces and parts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A chunk is a thick, solid piece of something, like a chunk of cheese. It can also mean a large part or amount, like a chunk of time. Look at the words around it to find which meaning fits. «Long words are read chunk by chunk, sand-wich.» Here the pieces are small parts of a word, so chunk means a part.
explain: As a verb, to chunk means to break something into smaller parts. Look for a clue that something is being split up. «Messages are turned into bits and split into packets, small chunks of data.» Split and chunks both show that something big has been broken into smaller pieces.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Its famous rings are countless chunks of water ice, from tiny grains to pieces as big as a house.» Try "pieces" in place of chunks: the sentence still makes sense, so chunks means pieces, and the list shows they can be very different sizes.
fact: A chunk can be a noun (a chunk, chunks) or a verb (to chunk, chunking).
fact: «Chunk» means a thick, solid piece of something, or a large part or amount of something.
fact: «A good chunk of» means a large part of something.
fact: In maths, chunking is a way of dividing by taking away groups, such as 10 lots of 7.
fact: In reading, you can chunk a long word into smaller parts to help you read it, like sand-wich.
exercise: «She ate a big chunk of the cake.» What does chunk mean here? | A sharp knife | A baking tin | *A thick, solid piece of cake | A loud noise
exercise: «Messages are turned into bits and split into packets, small chunks of data.» Find one word that means the same as broken into pieces. | packets | bits | *split | data
exercise: Ali divides 70 by 7 using chunking. He takes away 10 lots of 7. What is chunking in maths? | A kind of times table song | A way of adding up all the numbers | *A way of dividing by taking away groups | A method for drawing shapes
test: «A good chunk of the day was spent waiting.» What does a good chunk of mean? | Nothing at all | A plate of food | A small, tiny amount of | *A large part of
test: «Its rings are countless chunks of water ice, from tiny grains to pieces as big as a house.» What does this tell us about chunks? | They are only found on Earth | They are made of wood | They are all exactly the same size | *They can be very different sizes
exam: «The crocodile twisted off a chunk of meat.» Which meaning of chunk fits best here? | *A thick, solid piece | To be very fast | A type of bird | A tiny drop of water
